%% Chart of tests/tla/tool_bridge/AgentWait.tla, the design that agent-design.cfg checks (it passes).
%% Labels use bash call, the words the person sees, and never write a model variable as a variable.
stateDiagram-v2
    state "No program is running" as NoProgram
    state "The program runs inside its first bash call" as FirstRun
    state "The program is waiting for a subagent, and the bash call is held" as Waiting
    state "A report waits for your turn while fx is inside the bash call" as ReportHeld
    state "The bash call returned still running" as Yielded
    state "fx waits again for the program (wait_more); the bridge is gone, so a wait is refused at once" as LaterRun
    state "The program has ended; the bash call returns once its bridge calls end" as GoneHeld
    state "The program ended while its wait was still open" as GoneWaiting

    [*] --> NoProgram
    NoProgram --> FirstRun : the model starts a program
    FirstRun --> Waiting : the program sends fx tool agent wait while a subagent works
    FirstRun --> ReportHeld : a subagent posts a report
    FirstRun --> Yielded : the bash call yields after its yield time
    FirstRun --> GoneHeld : the program exits or is killed
    Waiting --> ReportHeld : a subagent posts a report; the wait ends and leaves the report for your turn
    Waiting --> GoneWaiting : the program exits or is killed
    GoneWaiting --> GoneHeld : fx cancels the wait of the exited program
    ReportHeld --> Yielded : the bash call yields after its yield time
    ReportHeld --> GoneHeld : the program exits or is killed
    Yielded --> LaterRun : the model asks for more time on the bash call
    Yielded --> Yielded : a report joins your turn
    Yielded --> Yielded : the program sends fx tool agent wait, and it is refused at once
    LaterRun --> Yielded : the bash call yields again
    LaterRun --> GoneHeld : the program exits or is killed
    GoneHeld --> NoProgram : the bash call returns

    note right of Waiting
        Rule NoYieldWhileHeld breaks here, and only in agent-mutant-yield-while-held, a planted bug.
        The bash call yields while the wait holds it.
        Shortest path, the same as the TLC trace: the program starts, sends the wait, then the bash call yields.
        Actions: Run, StartWait, Yield.
    end note

    note right of GoneWaiting
        Rule NoMailLost breaks on the step "a subagent posts a report" out of this state, and only in agent-mutant-takes-mail, the rejected design.
        The wait takes the report, the program is gone, and the report is dropped.
        TLC trace actions: Run, StartWait, Gone, Post.
        Rule WaitEndsWhenGone breaks here, and only in agent-mutant-ignore-cancel, a planted bug.
        The cancel is ignored, so the wait never ends. It is the only failing config that checks this rule.
        TLC trace actions: Run, Yield, Gone, Post, Join, Run, StartWait, Gone, then a stutter.
        Shorter path to this state: Run, StartWait, Gone.
        Rule CallReturnsWhenGone breaks here, and only in agent-mutant-ignore-cancel-hang, a planted bug.
        The bash call never returns, because the wait never ends.
        TLC trace actions: Post, Run, Yield, Join, StartWait, Post, Join, Gone, Run, StartWait, Gone, then a stutter.
        Shorter path to this state: Run, StartWait, Gone.
    end note

%% Left out of this chart:
%% - A subagent finishes its work. The chart keeps a subagent that can still post.
%% - A wait that returns at once, because a report is already ready or no subagent works. Only a wait that holds is drawn.
%% - The answer a wait gives the program: a report, quiet, canceled, or refused. Only the resulting states are drawn.
%% - The program exits after its bash call yielded, and a new program starts from there.
%% - A report that joins your turn after the bash call has returned and no program runs.
%% - Caps on how many reports, runs, and wait requests there can be.
%% - Fairness: fx steps happen eventually, while the program, the subagent, and the model may stop at any time.
